      players: 'Four active players. Five can participate with dealer sitting out each hand.',
      deck: 'Standard Austrian 54-card Tarock pack: 22 trumps (Tarocks), 8 cards each in four suits.',
      equipment: 'Standard Austrian 54-card Tarock pack: 22 trumps (Tarocks), 8 cards each in four suits.',
      dealing: "Dealer shuffles, player to left cuts. Deal 12 cards to each player in batches of 6, anticlockwise, starting with player to dealer's right. Place two packets of 3 cards face down in middle as talon.",
    },
    turnFlow: "Dealer deals 12 cards each and 6 to the talon. Players bid (Sechserdreier, Rufer mit Spatz/Uhu, Dreier) or say Erster; if all pass, Fahren is played. Bidder calls a King (in Rufer) or takes 3 or 6 talon cards and discards. Announcements and Kontras follow. Player to dealer's right leads; 12 tricks, follow suit, must trump if unable to follow. Highest trump wins trick, else highest of led suit. Team with 36+ of 71 card points wins the game; bonuses and game points are settled in cash.",
