      'Setup example: 12 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Win tricks containing valuable cards. In positive contracts, need 36+ of 71 card points. Various contracts have different objectives.',
      "Turn-flow example: Dealer deals 12 cards each and 6 to the talon. Players bid (Sechserdreier, Rufer mit Spatz/Uhu, Dreier) or say Erster; if all pass, Fahren is played. Bidder calls a King (in Rufer) or takes 3 or 6 talon cards and discards. Announcements and Kontras follow. Player to dealer's right leads; 12 tricks, follow suit, must trump if unable to follow. Highest trump wins trick, else highest of led suit. Team with 36+ of 71 card points wins the game; bonuses and game points are settled in cash.",
      'Scoring example: Card points counted individually (not in groups). Total 71 points, need 36+ to win. Game points and bonuses calculated separately. Win majority of 71 card points (36 or more) in tricks; contract and bonuses determine game points paid between teams..',
